      fit cancels the wiring's level term at ONE value of it (`w_in` 0.12). If the level moves across these
      bands, no constant `w_in` cancels it everywhere and the wiring is right at one distance from home.
      READ THE TOP ROW'S SHARE. `(AtNest, Drop, 1.0889)` against `(Bias, Drop, -0.2)` puts P(drop) at
      EXACTLY 0 anywhere below adjacency, at any crop fill. So a small top row means the ants never
      REACH the comb, and a large one with few drops would mean they reach it and decline.
